  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{I}_3^{-}$is linear with central iodine atom undergoing $s p^3 d$-hybridisation and three lone pairs occupying equatorial position.\nThus, this structure include $d$-orbital contribution to the hybridisation scheme.\nThe structure is,\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/BG4fY7jMOsB4UjCF25RtcpyFgdhDzJBTzNjMAZ5Xdp8.original.fullsize.png\"/>\n$\\mathrm{PCl}_3$ structure is $s p^3$-hybridised with one lone pair.\n$\\mathrm{NO}_3^{-}$is $s p^2$-hybridised and $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{Se}$ is $s p^3$ - hybridised with two lone pairs of Se atom.",
    "image": null
  },
